---
/*
  /admin/: the admin app. Jeff signs in with his Bluesky account (AT Protocol OAuth) and changes
  the site's records in his own repo: the status, drafts, the pages' content and the lexicons. All of it
  runs in the browser (src/lib/admin/app.ts); there's no server or database behind it. Installs
  as a PWA. Kept out of search engines and the sitemap.
*/
import Admin from '~/layouts/admin.astro';
import { EMOJI_PICKS, STATES, STATE_INFO, toneColour } from '~/lib/status-states.mjs';
---

<Admin title="Admin · Skiddle">
  <div class="admin">
    <header class="admin-bar">
      <a href="/" class="admin-home"><span>skiddle@admin</span><span class="cursor-blink" aria-hidden="true"></span></a>
      <div id="account" class="admin-account" hidden>
        <span id="accountHandle" class="admin-muted"></span>
        <button id="signOut" type="button" class="admin-btn admin-btn-ghost">Sign out</button>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main id="main" class="admin-main">
      <h1 class="sr-only">skiddle.id admin</h1>
      <p id="loading" class="admin-muted" role="status">Loading…</p>
      <p id="notice" class="admin-notice" role="alert" hidden></p>

      <section id="signedOut" class="admin-card" aria-labelledby="signInTitle" hidden>
        <h2 id="signInTitle">Sign in</h2>
        <p>
          Sign in with your Bluesky account, <strong>@skiddle.blue</strong>. On Bluesky's page you approve what this app may
          change: your posts and drafts with their images, series, the pages' content, your status and the lexicons you publish,
          plus new Bluesky posts that announce your posts. It can't edit or delete anything else on Bluesky.
        </p>
        <button id="signIn" type="button" class="admin-btn admin-btn-primary">Sign in with Bluesky</button>
        <p class="admin-small">
          You stay signed in on this device only. What the app saves are public records in your AT Protocol repo.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="wrongAccount" class="admin-card" aria-labelledby="wrongTitle" hidden>
        <h2 id="wrongTitle">Not this account</h2>
        <p>You signed in as <code id="wrongDid"></code>. This admin only changes skiddle.id, which belongs to @skiddle.blue.</p>
        <button type="button" class="admin-btn" data-sign-out>Sign out</button>
      </section>

      <div id="signedIn" hidden>
      <div id="dashboard" class="admin-stack" data-section="posts">
        <nav id="sectionNav" class="admin-sections" aria-label="Sections">
          <a href="#posts" data-section="posts" aria-current="page">Posts</a>
          <a href="#series" data-section="series">Series</a>
          <a href="#pages" data-section="pages">Pages</a>
          <a href="#status" data-section="status">Status</a>
          <a href="#timeline" data-section="timeline">Timeline</a>
          <a href="#site" data-section="site">Site</a>
        </nav>

        <section class="admin-card" data-section="posts" aria-labelledby="postsTitle">
          <div class="admin-label-row">
            <h2 id="postsTitle">Posts</h2>
            <span class="admin-toolbar">
              <a href="#page/categories" class="admin-btn admin-btn-ghost">Categories</a>
              <button id="newDraft" type="button" class="admin-btn admin-btn-ghost">New draft</button>
            </span>
          </div>
          <div id="postsScope" class="admin-notice" hidden>
            <p>To write drafts, upload images, publish, edit categories and publish Bluesky feeds, the app needs more permissions from your account.</p>
            <button id="postsSignIn" type="button" class="admin-btn">Sign in again</button>
          </div>
          <h3 class="admin-subhead">Drafts</h3>
          <ul id="drafts" class="admin-list"><li class="admin-muted">Loading…</li></ul>
          <details class="admin-details">
            <summary>Published (<span id="publishedCount">…</span>)</summary>
            <ul id="published" class="admin-list"></ul>
          </details>
          <p class="admin-small">Drafts are saved to your repo as you type, so they’re on all your devices. Anyone who looks can read them there, as with drafts in git today.</p>
          <p id="postsMessage" class="admin-message" role="status"></p>
        </section>

        <section class="admin-card" data-section="series" aria-labelledby="seriesTitle">
          <div class="admin-label-row">
            <h2 id="seriesTitle">Series</h2>
            <a href="#new-series" class="admin-btn admin-btn-ghost">New series</a>
          </div>
          <ul id="seriesList" class="admin-list"><li class="admin-muted">Loading…</li></ul>
          <p id="seriesNotLive" class="admin-small" hidden></p>
          <p id="seriesMessage" class="admin-message" role="status"></p>
        </section>

        <section class="admin-card" data-section="pages" aria-labelledby="pagesTitle">
          <h2 id="pagesTitle">Pages</h2>
          <p>The site’s metadata for search engines, the home page, the CV, services, uses, About, Now, Notes and the projects: records in your repo, which the site’s pages read. Open one to edit it.</p>
          <div id="pagesScope" class="admin-notice" hidden>
            <p>To write the pages’ records, the app needs more permissions from your account.</p>
            <button id="pagesSignIn" type="button" class="admin-btn">Sign in again</button>
          </div>
          <h3 class="admin-subhead">One record per page</h3>
          <ul id="pagesList" class="admin-lexicons admin-pages"><li class="admin-muted">Loading…</li></ul>
          <div class="admin-label-row">
            <h3 class="admin-subhead">One record per project</h3>
            <a href="#new-project" class="admin-btn admin-btn-ghost">New project</a>
          </div>
          <ul id="projectsList" class="admin-lexicons admin-pages"></ul>
          <p id="pagesMessage" class="admin-message" role="status"></p>
          <p class="admin-small">Records are public, like the pages, and go further: other services can keep copies even after a delete.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="admin-card" data-section="status" aria-labelledby="statusTitle">
          <h2 id="statusTitle">Your status</h2>
          <div id="statusScope" class="admin-notice" hidden>
            <p>To keep each status in your history, the app needs one more permission from your account.</p>
            <button id="statusSignIn" type="button" class="admin-btn">Sign in again</button>
          </div>
          <p class="admin-preview" aria-live="polite">
            <span id="previewDot" class="admin-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span id="previewEmoji" class="admin-preview-emoji" aria-hidden="true" hidden></span>
            <span id="previewText"></span>
          </p>
          <form id="statusForm" class="admin-form" novalidate>
            <fieldset class="admin-segment">
              <legend>Status</legend>
              {
                STATES.map((state, i) => (
                  <label>
                    <input type="radio" name="state" value={state} checked={i === 0} />
                    <span class="admin-dot" style={`background: ${toneColour(STATE_INFO[state].tone)}`} aria-hidden="true" />
                    <span>{STATE_INFO[state].label}</span>
                  </label>
                ))
              }
            </fieldset>
            <div class="admin-field">
              <div class="admin-label-row">
                <label for="statusText">What it says</label>
                <span id="statusCount" class="admin-muted" aria-live="polite">0/64</span>
              </div>
              <input id="statusText" name="text" type="text" required maxlength="640" autocomplete="off" placeholder="open to consulting" aria-describedby="statusCount" />
            </div>
            <div class="admin-field">
              <label for="statusEmoji">Emoji</label>
              <input id="statusEmoji" name="emoji" type="text" maxlength="64" autocomplete="off" placeholder="None: the coloured dot" aria-describedby="statusEmojiHelp" />
              <div class="admin-emoji-picks" role="group" aria-label="Quick picks">
                {EMOJI_PICKS.map((e) => <button type="button" class="admin-btn admin-btn-ghost" data-emoji={e} aria-label={`Use ${e}`}>{e}</button>)}
                <button type="button" class="admin-btn admin-btn-ghost" data-emoji="">No emoji</button>
              </div>
              <p id="statusEmojiHelp" class="admin-small">One emoji, shown instead of the dot on the site and the badge. Leave it empty for the dot.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="admin-field">
              <label for="statusLocation">Location</label>
              <input id="statusLocation" name="location" type="text" maxlength="640" autocomplete="off" placeholder="Bangkok" />
            </div>
            <div class="admin-field">
              <label for="statusTimeZone">Time zone</label>
              <select id="statusTimeZone" name="timeZone">
                <option value="Asia/Bangkok">Asia/Bangkok</option>
              </select>
              <button id="useDeviceZone" type="button" class="admin-link" hidden></button>
            </div>
            <button id="statusSave" type="submit" class="admin-btn admin-btn-primary">Save status</button>
            <p id="statusMessage" class="admin-message" role="status"></p>
          </form>
          <p id="statusUpdated" class="admin-small"></p>
          <h3 class="admin-subhead">History</h3>
          <p class="admin-small">Each status you save is kept, newest first. <a href="/status/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">See them all on /status/</a>.</p>
          <ul id="statusHistory" class="admin-lexicons admin-pages"><li class="admin-muted">Loading…</li></ul>
          <p id="statusHistoryMessage" class="admin-message" role="status"></p>
        </section>

        <section class="admin-card" data-section="timeline" aria-labelledby="timelineTitle">
          <div class="admin-label-row">
            <h2 id="timelineTitle">Timeline</h2>
            <span class="admin-toolbar">
              <a id="newEvent" href="#new-event" class="admin-btn admin-btn-ghost">New event</a>
            </span>
          </div>
          <p>The events on <a href="/timeline/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">/timeline/</a>. Records are public, so until an event is over it holds only its kind, its days, its city and a general note, unless you tick Announced. Its title, times, place and link open once it’s over. Keep anything private off it.</p>
          <div id="timelineScope" class="admin-notice" hidden>
            <p>To write events, the app needs one more permission from your account.</p>
            <button id="timelineSignIn" type="button" class="admin-btn">Sign in again</button>
          </div>
          <h3 class="admin-subhead">Upcoming</h3>
          <ul id="timelineUpcoming" class="admin-lexicons admin-pages"><li class="admin-muted">Loading…</li></ul>
          <div id="timelineRoughSection" hidden>
            <h3 class="admin-subhead">Fill in the details</h3>
            <p class="admin-small">Over, and still only rough. Add what you’d like to show, or leave them as they are.</p>
            <ul id="timelineRough" class="admin-lexicons admin-pages"></ul>
          </div>
          <h3 class="admin-subhead">Past</h3>
          <ul id="timelinePast" class="admin-lexicons admin-pages"></ul>
          <p id="timelineMessage" class="admin-message" role="status"></p>
        </section>

        <section class="admin-card" data-section="site" aria-labelledby="lexiconTitle">
          <h2 id="lexiconTitle">Lexicons</h2>
          <p>
            They describe the site's records: the status, posts, series, drafts and the pages' content. Publishing them lets other apps look up and
            check the records' shape. They come from the site's <code>lexicons/</code> folder.
          </p>
          <ul id="lexicons" class="admin-lexicons"><li class="admin-muted">Checking…</li></ul>
          <button id="lexiconPublishAll" type="button" class="admin-btn" hidden>Publish all</button>
          <p id="lexiconMessage" class="admin-message" role="status"></p>
          <p id="lexiconDns" class="admin-small"></p>
        </section>

        <section class="admin-card" data-section="site" aria-labelledby="cardsTitle">
          <h2 id="cardsTitle">Share cards</h2>
          <p>
            Posts, series and scheduled drafts keep the share card drawn for them. After a change to the card design, check
            them: each one is drawn again and compared with the stored one. Nothing is saved until you press Save.
          </p>
          <button id="cardsCheck" type="button" class="admin-btn admin-self-start">Check share cards</button>
          <p id="cardsMessage" class="admin-message" role="status"></p>
          <ul id="cardsList" class="admin-list admin-cards"></ul>
          <button id="cardsSave" type="button" class="admin-btn admin-self-start" hidden>Save</button>
          <p id="cardsNotLive" class="admin-small" hidden></p>
        </section>

        <section class="admin-card" data-section="site" aria-labelledby="recordsTitle">
          <h2 id="recordsTitle">Records</h2>
          <p>What the site keeps in your repo: everything it shows.</p>
          <ul id="records" class="admin-records"><li class="admin-muted">Loading…</li></ul>
        </section>
      </div>

      <div id="editor" class="admin-editor" data-pane="write" data-kind="draft">
        <div class="admin-editor-bar">
          <a href="#posts" class="admin-btn admin-btn-ghost">← Posts</a>
          <div class="admin-bar-end">
            <span id="editorState" class="admin-save-state" aria-live="polite"></span>
            <button id="edFocus" type="button" class="admin-btn admin-btn-ghost" aria-pressed="false" title="Only the title and the text (Esc to leave)">Focus</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div id="editorConflict" class="admin-notice" hidden>
          <p>This draft was changed on another device since you opened it.</p>
          <button id="edLoadTheirs" type="button" class="admin-btn">Load that version</button>
          <button id="edKeepMine" type="button" class="admin-btn">Keep mine</button>
        </div>
        <div id="editorBackup" class="admin-notice" hidden>
          <p>This device has changes from <span id="edBackupTime"></span> that weren’t saved.</p>
          <button id="edRestore" type="button" class="admin-btn">Restore them</button>
          <button id="edDiscard" type="button" class="admin-btn">Discard</button>
        </div>
        <p id="editorMessage" class="admin-message" role="status"></p>

        <form id="editorForm" class="admin-form" novalidate>
          <div class="admin-field admin-field-title">
            <label for="edTitle">Title</label>
            <input id="edTitle" type="text" autocomplete="off" placeholder="Untitled" />
          </div>
          <div class="admin-field">
            <div class="admin-label-row">
              <label for="edDescription">Description</label>
              <span id="edDescriptionCount" class="admin-muted">0/300</span>
            </div>
            <textarea id="edDescription" rows="2" placeholder="One or two sentences for lists, feeds and share cards"></textarea>
          </div>
          <div class="admin-field">
            <label for="edSlug">Address</label>
            <div class="admin-affix"><span>/posts/</span><input id="edSlug" type="text" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" /><span>/</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="admin-row">
            <div class="admin-field">
              <label for="edCategory">Category</label>
              <select id="edCategory"></select>
            </div>
            <div class="admin-field">
              <label for="edLang">Language</label>
              <select id="edLang"></select>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="admin-field">
            <label for="edTags">Tags</label>
            <input id="edTags" type="text" autocomplete="off" placeholder="atproto, astro, homelab" />
          </div>
          <div class="admin-row">
            <div class="admin-field">
              <label for="edSeries">Series</label>
              <select id="edSeries"></select>
            </div>
            <div class="admin-field admin-field-narrow">
              <label for="edPart">Part</label>
              <input id="edPart" type="number" min="1" inputmode="numeric" />
            </div>
          </div>
          <label class="admin-check"><input id="edFeatured" type="checkbox" /> Featured on the home page</label>

          <div class="admin-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Editor">
            <button type="button" role="tab" data-pane="write" aria-selected="true">Write</button>
            <button type="button" role="tab" data-pane="preview" aria-selected="false">Preview</button>
          </div>
          <div class="admin-editor-panes">
            <div class="admin-pane-write">
              <div id="edTools" class="admin-toolbar admin-write-tools">
                <label class="admin-btn admin-btn-ghost">Add image<input id="edImage" type="file" accept="image/png,image/jpeg,image/webp,image/gif" class="sr-only" /></label>
              </div>
              <div id="edImageBox" class="admin-image-box" hidden>
                <img id="edImageThumb" alt="" />
                <div class="admin-field">
                  <label for="edImageAlt">Alt text</label>
                  <input id="edImageAlt" type="text" autocomplete="off" placeholder="What the image shows" />
                </div>
                <div class="admin-toolbar">
                  <button id="edImageUpload" type="button" class="admin-btn admin-btn-primary">Upload and insert</button>
                  <button id="edImageCancel" type="button" class="admin-btn">Cancel</button>
                </div>
              </div>
              <p id="edImageMessage" class="admin-message" role="status"></p>
              <label for="edMarkdown" class="sr-only">Post, in Markdown</label>
              <textarea id="edMarkdown" class="admin-markdown" spellcheck="true" placeholder="Write in Markdown… Paste or drop images here." aria-describedby="edWords"></textarea>
              <p id="edWords" class="admin-small admin-words"></p>
            </div>
            <div id="edPreviewPane" class="admin-pane-preview">
              <div class="admin-card-preview">
                <button id="edCard" type="button" class="admin-btn admin-btn-ghost">Show the share card</button>
                <img id="edCardImage" alt="The post’s share card" width="1200" height="630" hidden />
                <p id="edCardMessage" class="admin-message" role="status"></p>
              </div>
              <div id="edPreviewHead" class="admin-preview-head"></div>
              <div id="edPreview" class="prose prose-reading admin-preview-body"></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p id="editorProblems" class="admin-message" role="status"></p>

          <div class="admin-editor-actions">
            <button id="edPublish" type="button" class="admin-btn admin-btn-primary" data-for="draft" disabled>Publish</button>
            <button id="edFinish" type="button" class="admin-btn admin-btn-primary" data-for="draft" hidden>Finish publishing</button>
            <div class="admin-schedule" data-for="draft">
              <div class="admin-field">
                <label for="edPublishAt">Or publish it later</label>
                <input id="edPublishAt" type="datetime-local" aria-describedby="edZone" />
                <p id="edZone" class="admin-small"></p>
              </div>
              <div class="admin-toolbar">
                <button id="edSchedule" type="button" class="admin-btn" disabled>Schedule</button>
                <button id="edUnschedule" type="button" class="admin-btn" hidden>Unschedule</button>
              </div>
              <p id="edScheduled" class="admin-small admin-scheduled" hidden></p>
            </div>
            <label class="admin-check" data-for="post"><input id="edMinor" type="checkbox" /> Small fix: don’t mark the post as updated</label>
            <button id="edSavePost" type="button" class="admin-btn admin-btn-primary" data-for="post" disabled>Save changes</button>
            <p class="admin-small" data-not-live></p>
            <a id="edViewPost" href="/posts/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="admin-link" data-for="post">View the post</a>
            <button id="edDelete" type="button" class="admin-btn" data-for="draft">Delete draft</button>
            <button id="edUnpublish" type="button" class="admin-btn" data-for="post" disabled>Unpublish</button>
          </div>
        </form>
      </div>

      <div id="seriesEditor" class="admin-editor">
        <div class="admin-editor-bar">
          <a href="#series" class="admin-btn admin-btn-ghost">← Series</a>
          <span id="seState" class="admin-save-state" aria-live="polite"></span>
        </div>
        <div id="seConflict" class="admin-notice" hidden>
          <p>This series was changed on another device since you opened it.</p>
          <button id="seLoadTheirs" type="button" class="admin-btn">Load that version</button>
          <button id="seKeepMine" type="button" class="admin-btn">Keep mine</button>
        </div>
        <div id="seBackup" class="admin-notice" hidden>
          <p>This device has changes from <span id="seBackupTime"></span> that weren’t saved.</p>
          <button id="seRestore" type="button" class="admin-btn">Restore them</button>
          <button id="seDiscard" type="button" class="admin-btn">Discard</button>
        </div>
        <p id="seMessage" class="admin-message" role="status"></p>

        <form id="seForm" class="admin-form" novalidate hidden>
          <div class="admin-field">
            <label for="seName">Name</label>
            <input id="seName" type="text" autocomplete="off" placeholder="From Fear to Flight" aria-describedby="seKey" />
            <p id="seKey" class="admin-small"></p>
          </div>
          <div class="admin-field">
            <div class="admin-label-row">
              <label for="seDescription">Description</label>
              <span id="seDescriptionCount" class="admin-muted">0/300</span>
            </div>
            <textarea id="seDescription" rows="3" placeholder="What the series is about, for /series/ and its share card"></textarea>
          </div>
          <label class="admin-check"><input id="seOngoing" type="checkbox" /> Ongoing: no last part, like a weekly series</label>
          <div id="seCadenceField" class="admin-field">
            <label for="seCadence">How often new parts come out</label>
            <div class="admin-affix"><span>new&nbsp;</span><input id="seCadence" type="text" autocomplete="off" placeholder="every week" /></div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <label class="admin-check"><input id="seFeed" type="checkbox" aria-describedby="seFeedHint" /> RSS feed for this series</label>
            <p id="seFeedHint" class="admin-small"></p>
          </div>
          <fieldset id="seBluesky" class="admin-field" hidden>
            <legend class="admin-legend">Bluesky feed</legend>
            <p class="admin-small">A feed people can pin in Bluesky, of the posts that announce the series’ parts. It takes the series’ saved name and description.</p>
            <button id="seBlueskyPublish" type="button" class="admin-btn admin-btn-ghost admin-self-start">Publish a Bluesky feed</button>
            <a id="seBlueskyOpen" href="https://bsky.app/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="admin-link" hidden>Open in Bluesky</a>
            <p id="seBlueskyMessage" class="admin-message" role="status"></p>
          </fieldset>
          <fieldset class="admin-field">
            <legend class="admin-legend">Parts</legend>
            <ol id="seParts" class="admin-parts"></ol>
            <button id="seAddPart" type="button" class="admin-btn admin-btn-ghost admin-self-start">Add a planned part</button>
            <p class="admin-small">Planned parts show as “coming”. A published post with the same part number takes a planned part’s place.</p>
          </fieldset>
          <div class="admin-card-preview">
            <button id="seCard" type="button" class="admin-btn admin-btn-ghost">Show the share card</button>
            <img id="seCardImage" alt="The series’ share card" width="1200" height="630" hidden />
            <p id="seCardMessage" class="admin-message" role="status"></p>
          </div>
          <p id="seProblems" class="admin-message" role="status"></p>

          <div class="admin-editor-actions">
            <button id="seSave" type="button" class="admin-btn admin-btn-primary" disabled>Save series</button>
            <p id="seNotLive" class="admin-small" hidden></p>
            <p id="seOffSite" class="admin-small" hidden>A series shows on the site once its first part is published.</p>
            <a id="seView" href="/series/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="admin-link" hidden>View it on the site</a>
            <button id="seDelete" type="button" class="admin-btn" hidden>Delete series</button>
            <p id="seDeleteNote" class="admin-small" hidden></p>
          </div>
        </form>
      </div>

      <div id="pageEditor" class="admin-editor">
        <div class="admin-editor-bar">
          <a id="peBack" href="#pages" class="admin-btn admin-btn-ghost">← Pages</a>
          <span id="peState" class="admin-save-state" aria-live="polite"></span>
        </div>
        <h2 id="peTitle" class="admin-editor-title"></h2>
        <div id="peConflict" class="admin-notice" hidden>
          <p>This was changed on another device since you opened it.</p>
          <button id="peLoadTheirs" type="button" class="admin-btn">Load that version</button>
          <button id="peKeepMine" type="button" class="admin-btn">Keep mine</button>
        </div>
        <div id="peBackup" class="admin-notice" hidden>
          <p>This device has changes from <span id="peBackupTime"></span> that weren’t saved.</p>
          <button id="peRestore" type="button" class="admin-btn">Restore them</button>
          <button id="peDiscard" type="button" class="admin-btn">Discard</button>
        </div>
        <p id="peRough" class="admin-notice" hidden>Upcoming, so only its kind, its days, its city and its note are saved: records are public, so keep the note general. Its title, times, place and link open once it’s over. Tick Announced to make them public now.</p>
        <p id="peNote" class="admin-small" hidden>Not in your repo yet. Fill it in and save to create it.</p>
        <p id="peMessage" class="admin-message" role="status"></p>

        <form id="peForm" class="admin-form" novalidate hidden>
          <div id="peFields"></div>
          <p id="peKey" class="admin-small" hidden></p>
